{"total_count":1836,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/commits/a5e03889d689691a25c74807bab6d96546320000","sha":"a5e03889d689691a25c74807bab6d96546320000","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0NjU2MDA5NzU6YTVlMDM4ODlkNjg5NjkxYTI1Yzc0ODA3YmFiNmQ5NjU0NjMyMDAwMA==","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/a5e03889d689691a25c74807bab6d96546320000","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/commits/a5e03889d689691a25c74807bab6d96546320000/comments","commit":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/git/commits/a5e03889d689691a25c74807bab6d96546320000","author":{"date":"2026-05-20T21:21:02.000-07:00","name":"Edward Z. Yang","email":"ezyang@meta.com"},"committer":{"date":"2026-05-21T12:57:22.000Z","name":"PyTorch MergeBot","email":"pytorchmergebot@users.noreply.github.com"},"message":"Use PyTorch Min/Max in Inductor index propagation (#184589)\n\nSymPy's builtin Min/Max constructors run generic pairwise dominance checks in _find_localzeros via _is_connected. For dynamic avg_pool3d_backward CPU codegen, index propagation builds many boundary expressions containing Max(0, x - 1) and Min(s, Max(...) + k). During CPU vector tiling analysis those expressions are repeatedly substituted and simplified, and the builtin SymPy Min/Max path dominates compile time.\n\nUse torch.utils._sympy.functions.Min/Max for symbolic ops.minimum/maximum propagation, and for avg-pool divisor boundary construction. The PyTorch Min/Max implementation keeps the useful numeric 0/1 special cases but avoids the generic pairwise is-connected test.\n\nBenchmarks on test/inductor/test_torchinductor_codegen_dynamic_shapes.py::DynamicShapesCodegenCpuTests::test_avg_pool3d_backward2_dynamic_shapes_cpu:\n\n- Baseline OSS repro: 1 passed in 342.93s (pytest total 0:05:42).\n\n- Fresh-cache timed reproduction: test body 337.347s, total 352.308s.\n\n- Compile-time breakdown before: compile_inner 333.266s, GraphLowering.codegen 330.383s, Scheduler.codegen 313.728s, compile_file 1.583s.\n\n- SymPy instrumentation before: Min._find_localzeros 140.7s total, Max._find_localzeros 125.6s total, with ~294k Max(2 args) and ~162k Min(2 args) calls.\n\n- Global/custom Min/Max experiment: ~72s.\n\n- After this patch: 1 passed in 75.52s (0:01:15).\n\nAdditional validation:\n\n- python -m pytest test/inductor/test_torchinductor.py -k 'index_propagation and cpu' -q -s: 7 passed, 2558 deselected in 16.85s.\n\n- python -m pytest test/inductor/test_torchinductor_codegen_dynamic_shapes.py -k 'avg_pool3d and dynamic_shapes_cpu' -q -s: 3 passed, 2370 deselected, 1 xfailed in 80.10s.\n\nAuthored by Codex\n\nPull Request resolved: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/184589\nApproved by: https://github.com/eellison, https://github.com/laithsakka","tree":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/git/trees/0e0da75ef221e7a13c90b6a6df966c956170fe8b","sha":"0e0da75ef221e7a13c90b6a6df966c956170fe8b"},"comment_count":0},"author":{"login":"ezyang","id":13564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang","html_url":"https://github.com/ezyang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"pytorchmergebot","id":97764156,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdPDPA","avatar_url":"https://ava